The oldest official map in Munich brings to light exciting stories .
It is annoying when maps are not up to date .
This is something everyone knows , who has had to get excited , as the car @-@ Navi showed a green meadow instead of a bypass .
The historical maps of the digital Bayern @-@ Atlas , an offer of the Bavarian Geoportal of the State Government , are anything but current - but for this reason , they are very informative .
Especially when you compare them to current online @-@ cards .
Then it becomes clear how the cities and municipalities in the area of distribution of the city of Merkur have changed since the 19th century .
The digital Bayern @-@ Atlas is a patch @-@ up that you can &apos;t see as such .
More detailed maps , so @-@ called primetization sheets , have been added to the large overview map for cities and municipalities .
According to the Bavarian Survey Administration , these were created between 1810 and 1864 and are the result of the first survey of Bavaria .
Your client : Napoleon .
The French army leader occupied Bavaria with Austria since the spring of 1800 during the Second Coalition War .
Napoleon wanted to have an overview of the occupied land and commissioned a topographic recording of Bavaria - for military purposes , of course .
Even if the French troops eventually withdrew with the peace of Lunéville on 9 February 1801 : It was the present @-@ day neighbours who created the idea of a nationwide map of Bavaria .
The project was driven forward by the courtesy of Max IV , the founder of the &quot; Topographical Bureau &quot; - and thus the Bavarian Survey Administration .
The Munich primordial is from 1856 and can be found like all other on the website of the Bavarian Landesbibliothek .
The comparison of the former and the present is the most impressive in the example of the capital of the province .
The city has expanded in all directions and has grown together .
An example of this is Untersendling , which appears in a relatively isolated way in the map of 1856 .
Sendling was incorporated as a district of Munich 21 years after the card was created , i.e. in 1877 .
Today Untersendling is in the centre of the city .
The Untersendling houses are concentrated around 1856 along the current Plinganserstrasse , which was named only in 1878 after Georg Sebastian Plinganser , a leader of the Bavarian farmer &apos;s revolt against Austria in 1705 .
The Westpark is the place where you can see nothing but fields - at first glance : a more small map with dozens of lines and numbers is shown in the zoom in : handwritten numbered plots from the so called &quot; primeval &quot; from where the land tax was derived .
Today , small plots are no longer occupied by farmers in the area , but by the small gardeners of the &quot; Land in Sun &quot; plant .
A large green area is being developed in the north of Untersendling .
The Theresienwiese , which was the location of the Oktoberfest since 1810 , was in fact a meadow in the 19th century - and not a concrete desert .
On the other hand , the historical map gives an insight into the history of psychiatric medicine .
In the area of the present district of Au @-@ Haidhausen , the original position sheet reads not only the street name &quot; am Gasteig &quot; or from the &quot; Am Lüfte &quot; ( on the air ) , but also in the letters &quot; Erren Anstalt . &quot;
Yes , here on the Auerfeldstrasse people were once locked in with delusions .
In 1858 / 59 the Munich District Irrenanstalt &quot; Auf der Auer Lüften &quot; was founded .
From 1872 , Dr. Bernhard von Gudden was in charge of the establishment - the psychiatrist brought in connection with the death of King Ludwig II .
&quot; He was a step forward for his time and , for example , ended the chaining of the so @-@ called &quot; mis<unk> . &quot;
He also prohibited the personnel from using violence against the occupants , &quot; says Hermann Wilhelm , Head of the Museum Haidhausen , who dealt with the institution for an exhibition .
The first place was 280 patients , and the second was 500 patients .
Eventually , this capacity was no longer sufficient - the reason for the construction of the regional irrigation plant in Haar in 1905 .
Since 2006 , the Isar @-@ Amper @-@ Klinikum Munich @-@ Ost is located there , one of the largest psychiatrist in Germany .
At the former Auer Anstalt area , youth meet now at the Salesianum in Munich .
The order purchased the building complex in 1920 and transformed it into a youth hostel with training facilities .
To the west lies the football field of the TSV München Ost , east houses from the 1980s .
In 2015 , the children &apos;s house &quot; Casa Don Bosco &quot; was built in architectural style , which was built in the Irrendize , which was destroyed during World War II .
The Marienplatz square was named &quot; Main Square &quot; around 1856 , the Kaufinger street was called &quot; Kaufinger Gasse . &quot;
