The National Association for the Promotion of Colorants has issued a warning to colored people who travel to Missouri on the grounds of the discriminatory policies and racist attacks of the state .
&quot; The NAACP Travel Advisory for the state of Missouri , which is to come into force by August 28 , 2017 , calls on afro @-@ American travelers , visitors and missourians to pay special attention to travel through the state and to exercise extreme caution , as a series of questionable racial @-@ based events are taking place in the whole state recently and are being noted here , &quot; the group states .
A recently passed Missouri law making it more difficult for people to win discrimination actions , as well as the state law enforcement authorities that disproportionately target minorities , prompted the group to issue the travel warning , said the NAACP .
&quot; They have violated civil rights that people pass .
They are stopped for their skin colour , they are beaten or killed , &quot; the President of the Missouri NAACP , Rod Chapel , the Kansas City Star said .
&quot; We hear complaints in such a frequency that we have not yet heard . &quot;
