Pearson cuts a further 3,000 jobs and cuts the dividend to revive the business .
The Pearson education group in the UK said on Friday that it would cut a further 3,000 jobs and reduce its interim dividend by 72 percent , as a further restructuring programme was being launched to overcome the pressure the company is facing .
The job cuts , which the General Director John Fallon announced for the most part for the end of 2018 and the beginning of 2019 , are in addition to his previous restructuring , which already lost 4,000 jobs .
Pearson announced in May a third cost reduction program a cost reduction plan of another £ 300m ( $ 394 million ) to revive a business that was taken by the rapid digital learning step .
The company , which sold its stake in Penguin Random House to Bertelsmann last month , said that the outlook for the financial year was unchanged , after reaching an increase of 1 percent to £ 2.05 billion in the first half of the year .
Kabul Convoi @-@ attack : Nato @-@ soldier killed in suicide bombing .
A suicide bomber attacked a military convoy in the Afghan capital Kabul , killed a NATO soldier and injured several others , say officials .
Five soldiers and an interpreter were injured , a declaration of NATO announced .
According to unconfirmed local reports , three civilians also died in the Qarabagh district .
The bombing is the last violence Afghanistan has taken this month - on Tuesday more than 30 people were killed in a mosque in Herat .
On Monday , a suicide bomber killed two people near the Iraqi Embassy in Kabul .
In a statement by the NATO , the explosion was on Thursday evening , when a joint patrol with the Afghan army was attacked by an &quot; improvised explosive device &quot; carried by people .
The statement states that all the injured are in a stable state and are treated in the US Military Hospital at the Bagram airfield .
Correspondents say that the growing strength of the Taliban and the group known as the so @-@ called Islamic State ( IS ) in Qarabagh is a great concern for NATO troops in the nearby Bagram .
According to the United Nations , at least 1,662 people died in Afghanistan in the first half of 2017 , of whom about 20 % were in the capital .
At the end of July , a suicide car bomb killed at least 30 people in a mainly Shiite district of Kabul .
The Taliban said they had carried out this attack .
On May 31st , a massive bombing in the city centre killed more than 150 people with the most deadly militant attack in the country , since the US @-@ led troops supplanted the Taliban in 2001 .
The violence underlines the precarious security situation in Afghanistan , as US President Donald Sturm is weighing up the number of US troops supporting the military and police in the country .
Correspondents say that the suicide attacks in Kabul in recent weeks have also caused a crisis of public trust in the government , its policies and in particular in the reputation of President Ashraf Ghani .
EPO returns decision to delay the smog rule after complaints to the effect that the ban on the smog is not enforced .
The US Environmental Protection Agency has suspended a decision to delay the Obama administration &apos;s regulation , which requires the States to reduce the emissions of smog , one day after 15 countries sued the agency for the action .
The EPO announced the decision to push the so @-@ called &quot; Ozon Regulations 2015 &quot; late on Wednesday and said that it would indicate the agency &apos;s commitment to work with countries .
&quot; We believe in dialogue with and in the fact that we are responding to our government partners , &quot; EPO Chairman Scott Pruitt said in a statement .
Pruitt announced in June the EPO &apos;s intention to delay the ozone regulations - which will measure pollutant emissions in a part of the country to determine where cuts must be made in order to meet more stringent air quality standards .
A group of 15 mostly democratic states , together with the district of Colombia , filed a complaint on Tuesday and said that the effort was illegal .
The government of President Donald SEN has attempted to reduce a wide range of environmental requirements that former President Barack Obama has imposed as part of a wider agenda that , according to the US Secretary of Economic Affairs , is intended to boost economic growth .
