Minister of Agriculture in the interview - How do we protect ourselves from poisons , Mr Schmidt ?
Germany is talking about contaminated eggs .
How could the scandal happen ?
How can consumers protect themselves .
The Minister of Agriculture , Christian Schmidt ( CSU ) , is in an interview with the German Editorial Network ( RND ) .
Mr. Schmidt , How can the consumer protect himself from poisoned eggs ?
I can only encourage all consumers to take a close look at the eggs in your fridge and check the stamp .
The Federal States will publish the latest information on the egg fees concerned on the consumer protection portal www.Food Warung.de .
Affected eggs should be destroyed or returned .
Even if , according to all we know at the moment , a health risk is practically impossible .
Will Aldi now assume the best possible crisis reaction - all eggs from the offer - because the Federal Minister of Agriculture does not really perceive the central role of the educator ?
Food monitoring is the task of the Federal States .
Nevertheless , my house was immediately opened and has been in close contact with the authorities of the countries since the German government was first announced .
All information and risk assessment are available to the consumer .
The trade , like the manufacturers , has to ensure that the products sold are marketable and do not pose any health risks .
If eggs exceed the maximum residue content of 0.005mg / kg , they are not marketable .
