Italy sharpenes the tone to NGO migrants rescue boats .
Italy has warned NGOs that use rescue boats for migrants in the Mediterranean that they should not continue this if they do not comply with new rules for their operations .
&quot; If NGOs do not sign a new code of conduct , it is difficult to see how they can continue to work , &quot; said Minister of the Interior Marco Minniti in an interview with the Turin newspaper La Stampa .
Minnitis warning came a day after the Italian authorities seized a boat from the German charity &apos; Jugend Retrett &apos; , because their team had been working effectively with human @-@ smugglers in a way that facilitated illegal immigration .
