Lavender from Provence threatened by climate change
It has become a symbol of Provence in the south of France , but there is a warning that it is threatened by climate change .
The lavender is declining because of the drought @-@ like conditions and the insects that transmit the diseases , which causes great headaches for scientists and farmers trying to find solutions .
Eric Chaisse , expert in the research institute for the agricultural sector of Provence , said : &quot; The lavender in Provence is in effective danger , as the plant in recent years has been exposed to the effects of climate change , which has caused much less rain in the spring and much more in the autumn .
This has an impact on the lifetime of the lavender .
There is also a small Zicade , a microbacterium that transmits dwargzicadas , and in very dry weather there are many of them . &quot;
And there is a lot at stake .
Lavender oil is not only a source of inspiration for tourists , but also a source of inspiration for perfumes and cosmetics .
Eric Chaisse said , &quot; Instead of having very long plant ears with a large number of flowers , we have smaller , underdeveloped and either missing or weakened .
So we have less parts with essential oil . &quot;
Solutions that are considered include better water distribution and slowing down evaporation from the soil , but also spraying plants with a protective mixture of sound and water and developing varieties that are more resistant to drought .
