&quot; We will close the WADA @-@ Timetable in the near future &quot; - the Russian Deputy Prime Minister Mutko .
The Russian Vice Premier Vitaly Mutko said it will not take long to implement the remaining criteria of the World Anti @-@ Doping Agency ( WADA ) for the restoration of the Russian anti @-@ doping agency ( RUSADA ) .
&quot; At a certain stage of meeting the criteria of the roadmap , RUSADA has been granted the right to plan and test in collaboration with UKAD ( UK anti @-@ doping ) .
The WADA timetable was updated in this respect , &quot; explained Mutko on Thursday .
The PM commented on the second part of the WADA compliance road map , which describes the criteria for the redeployment of RUSADA and was recently published on the organization &apos;s website .
According to Mutko , it contains nothing that could cause Russia to worry .
