And the results will be presented to the International Olympic Committee ( IOC ) and the WADA in the near future , &quot; he added .
One of the criteria stated in the list , however , states that the Russian anti @-@ doping authorities must publicly accept the reported findings of the WADA @-@ approved investigation by the Canadian attorney Richard McLaren on alleged state @-@ sponsored dopings in Russian sports .
Regarding the matter , Mutko said : &quot; We are conducting the investigation , as our anti @-@ doping system has admitted a bug .
All the measures have been implemented .
But there were no state programs and we will not admit anything that does not exist . &quot;
Mutkos &apos; words were in line with those of Vitaly Smirnov , the head of the independent Russian Anti @-@ Doping Commission .
In discussion with the Russian RSport sales office at the beginning of the day , Smirnov added problems of the past in Russian anti @-@ doping organizations , but then added : &quot; We have repeatedly said that the report contains controversial positions and regulations .
Nobody intends to accept this report unconditionally , &quot; added Smirnov .
In November 2015 , RUSADA was expelled from the WADA in the course of the doping scandal to carry out doping controls in Russia .
