Software update for Diesel Vehicles : What the persons concerned need to know now .
How exactly is the software update taking place ?
Do diesel drivers have to participate in the campaign ?
The most important questions and answers in a nutshell .
At the Diesel Summit , BMW , Daimler , Opel and the VW Group offered software updates for a total of around 5.3 million cars .
They are intended to improve the exhaust behaviour of cars in the emission classes Euro 5 and partly Euro 6 .
Euro 4 diesel or worse are excluded from this .
Anja Smetanin of ACE Auto Club Europa gives an opinion :
Is the new action obliging ?
No , the negotiated software updates are voluntary .
&quot; The mandatory updates before this , &quot; says Anja Smetanin , only apply to the vehicles that have Schummelsoftware .
The retrofitting of the equipment was ordered by the Federal Office for the Protection of the Force ( KBA ) .
How and when will customers be informed about updates ?
The manufacturers have announced a rapid implementation in the next few months , but have not yet given a precise date .
Daimler has announced that it will write to any person concerned .
If an inspection is already due , the inspection will be done within the inspection framework .
How long should the overall refurbishment take ?
&quot; Hard to say , &quot; says Smetanin .
This depends on the commitment of the manufacturers and the political pressure .
&quot; Because we have seen , the car manufacturers are not acting voluntarily on the subject of the environment so far . &quot;
How long should the update take ?
The conversion itself could take only three to four hours in the workshop .
It can take a bit longer to get an appointment .
What do drivers who do not drive a car from BMW , Daimler , Opel and the VW Group do ?
The ACE is a good advice to wait .
Presumably foreign manufacturers would be following , according to Smetanin .
Are there any risks of a massive drop in the price of Euro 4 cars ?
The ACE is afraid of that .
But especially in the regions where there is the threat of a ban on driving .
In rural areas , there has not been any loss of value for older diesel .
The ACE is advising to wait for a sale .
