Fund for Local Kites III
If you want to renovate your old house , you can get help from the country soon .
On Wednesday , the Mayor Albert Schindler and three representatives of the German Public Administration ( STEG ) presented the project to the public .
At the beginning of the information event , Schindler gave a further look at the events that had taken place so far .
Since 1991 , there have been restoration areas in the area of the village of Empfingen .
At that time , in the redevelopment area I from 1991 to 2004 , the state Baden @-@ Württemberg has taken over two thirds of the total funding .
In the redevelopment area II from 2005 to 2016 , the subsidy was still 60 percent .
For Schindler , the restructuring of the building to date is a &quot; success project &quot; - it is , after all , important to promote the development of the building itself , and not just to develop new construction areas .
On April 4 , the Karlsruhe Government Office provided the information that there would be a redevelopment area III .
The sum of the funding is 833 333 Euro , of which 500,000 Euro would be paid from the country , the rest from the village Empfingen .
How is a redevelopment area created ?
According to Schindler , one will investigate where the &quot; really old &quot; houses are .
It also has a role to play , if there is any interest in remediing in the area to be planned .
If necessary , the borders of the region could be moved over again .
On Wednesday evening , the STEG represented Martin Keller , Gaby Pietzschmann and Sarah Gotzel .
Keller presented the contents of the Federal @-@ State programme &quot; Social City , &quot; in which the redevelopment would then be carried out .
The core of the programme are the revitalization of inner cities , the improvement of living and working conditions and the maintenance and expansion of the infrastructure .
The measures would be implemented on an object @-@ specific basis , i.e. per plot .
The area of restoration would then be defined as a statute .
The period of the authorization for the funds has been in operation since 1 January 2017 until 30 April 2026 .
However , the inventory would be carried out by the end of this year , before the end of the year , in which the persons involved in the restoration area would receive a questionnaire for filling out .
In November or December , the Statutes Decree should be made as far as possible , in order to start the remedial measures in the coming year .
Pietzschmann explained that each commune had to carry out the preliminary investigations in question .
It is a matter of assessing the structural deficiencies of the city and deciding when the restoration should be carried out and to what extent .
A redevelopment note will be added to the land registry for the respective land .
Pietzschmann promised that he would come to Empfingen and take a picture of the situation .
Gotzel stressed that the involvement of the stakeholders was a major success factor for the project .
Therefore , there will be questionnaires that will be sent to the citizens in the coming weeks and will be completed by the end of the summer holidays .
The yellow questionnaire is the &quot; building and land arc , &quot; which is concerned , among other things , with the construction condition and the redevelopment intentions .
In the grey questionnaire , the &quot; Housing and Housing Bow , &quot; information on the size , division and residents of a living room can be provided .
The blue &quot; company sheet &quot; is to be filled only if the building has offices .
However , it is important to note that Gotzel pointed out that a questionnaire that has been filled out is not also an application for funding .
In addition , new construction measures are not eligible for funding .
Schindler stressed that the distribution of funds is based on the &quot; greyhound principle &quot; - whoever comes first , first , will first be served .
You can &apos;t &quot; reserve &quot; any funds for later .
Finally , photos of the &quot; Zentrum II &quot; project were shown to make the present present &quot; tasty &quot; for the rest .
