GMB concern about investment in the McVitie plant in Glasgow .
A trade union wants to get a confirmation from the managers of the biscuit producer McVitie about the long @-@ term commitment to the production at its plant in Glasgow .
GMB Scotland said that the company had kept its silence about the future of investment at the Tollcross site .
More than 500 employees work in the plant , which , in addition to other products , manufactures Hobnobs and Rich Tea biscuits .
McVities owner Pladis said that he has invested more than 5 million pounds in the last years .
He added that employees and trade union representatives would be &quot; the first to know &quot; if their activities were to change .
In a letter to the company &apos;s branch manager , GMB Scotland McVitie &apos;s urged McVitie to &quot; express concerns that the financing of the modernization of production lines would not be promoted . &quot;
GMB Senior Organizer Drew Duffy , said : &quot; The fact that we cannot get any clarity from the general site manager about the business needs and investment plans for the future of Tollcross is a matter of great concern to our members .
Generations of families have worked here and the workforce is concentrated on the local community and the Glasgow metropolitan area , an important pillar for dignified employment in an area with high unemployment and social disadvantages .
Hence , in the perspective of jobs , wages and prosperity , and against the background of the &quot; Breathe , &quot; the rising costs of living and the chronic decline in production , the eastern end of Glasgow is in urgent need of a flourishing production presence at McVitie . &quot;
Pladis &quot; said : &quot; The branch manager at Tollcross only yesterday received a letter from GMB Scotland and the company will respond directly to it , as we value the continuous involvement of employees and trade union representatives .
Two months ago , we had a regular meeting with employees and GMB representatives at Tollcross , where some questions were discussed openly .
We discussed with the employees that we , like all companies operating in a highly competitive and uncertain economic climate , would continuously monitor our business - and this applies to all of our business divisions and locations - in order to remain competitive .
She added , &quot; In the last years we have invested more than 5 million pounds in our Tollcross site , especially in production lines and operational improvements .
We fully recognize the heritage of Tollcross as a production site and should our operations at the site change , the employees and their trade union representatives will be the first to know . &quot;
Did the PSG give the Barcelona warning of Neymar three years ago ?
La League side may regret their interest in Marco Verratti .
Paris Saint @-@ Germain will continue its persecution of Neymar after making an offer of £ 189 million to trigger its release clause , but did they warn Barcelona three years ago of the world record raid ?
The sensational approach has fuelled the transfer window in the summer , as the Ligue 1 club is ready to break the world record by more than twice the previous brand , with Paul Pogba returning for £ 89 million last season .
After finishing , Neymar will become the most expensive player in the world and the highest paid professional athlete in the world .
Barcelona is furious about the way in which Neymar has forced his way out , although a source near the Catalan Board insists that the club has always done its best to take care of it since its arrival from Santos in 2013 .
But was the football world warned three years ago by the PSG @-@ president of this prospect ?
When Manchester City expressed interest in the signing of Blaise Matuidi in 2014 , Nasser Al @-@ Khelaifi had a severe warning for any club that wanted to have one of the best players sign by PSG .
&quot; I &apos;m not concerned because they know that if they touch one of our players , then we will oppose them , we will contact their players , &quot; said Al @-@ Khelaifi .
&quot; We respect all clubs .
But if they try to have one of our players sign with them , this will have consequences . &quot;
Barcelona seems to have crossed this line , with the Spanish club expressing interest in the PSG @-@ midfield player Marco Verratti at the beginning of this summer .
PSG made it clear that they would not allow the International from Italy to leave in any circumstances , and Barcelona could feel the consequences of this interest by losing one of its price offers for Neymar .
